    {
      "sections": [
        {
          "kind": "intro",
          "paragraphs": [
            "Czech main signals combine **this signal's speed** (the lower yellow lamp, with light strips below the head: none = 40, yellow strip = 60, one green = 80, two green = 100 km/h) and **what the next signal shows** (the upper lamps): green = volno, yellow = výstraha (stop), slow-flashing yellow = expect 40, fast-flashing yellow = expect 60, slow-flashing green = expect 80, fast-flashing green = expect 100. The **LS** cab system repeats the signals where the track carries codes; **Liberec – Stará Paka has no codes**, so there it only checks your vigilance. Speeds in km/h. Quadrant controls are from TheJAG's ČD 750 and 843 profiles."
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "systems",
          "title": "Safety systems",
          "cols": 2,
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "LS (LS 90 · LS IV / LVZ)",
              "full": "Liniový vlakový zabezpečovač",
              "summary": "On coded track the cab repeater shows the next signal: green, yellow, yellow ring (reduced speed), red; **blue = no vigilance press needed**. A more restrictive code asks for a press. On uncoded track (this route) it runs the vigilance check only.",
              "where": "843: LS 90. 750: LS IV type LVZ (same behaviour)",
              "quadrant": "843: left aux = LS 90 (On / Isolated); 750: left aux = LVZ (Active / Off)"
            },
            {
              "name": "Vigilance",
              "full": "Kontrola bdělosti",
              "summary": "When the **blue lamp goes out**, press the vigilance button within about **7 s**; then a **siren** for 5 s more, then the emergency brake. The checks pause while the loco brake is applied.",
              "where": "ČD 750 and 843",
              "quadrant": "**Gear lever** = vigilance button"
            }
          ]
