        {
          "kind": "howto",
          "title": "How to drive under LS and the vigilance check",
          "cols": 3,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "title": "On this route (no codes)",
              "steps": [
                "Drive to the lineside signals; the repeater shows no code.",
                "When the **blue lamp goes out**, press **vigilance** (gear lever) within about 7 s.",
                "Missed, the siren sounds: you have 5 s more, then the emergency brake."
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "After an LS emergency brake",
              "steps": [
                "Stop.",
                "843: switch LS 90 off and on (left aux twice).",
                "750: switch the LVZ off and on at the console in the engine room (or the left aux), then release the brake."
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "With LS codes (main lines)",
              "bullets": [
                "The repeater shows the next signal: green, yellow, yellow ring (reduced speed), red.",
                "Blue lit: no press needed.",
                "A more restrictive code: press **vigilance** at once, then brake to the signal."
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "Before departure",
              "steps": [
                "Loco brake fully applied.",
                "Train protection to **Start**, wait for the start lamp, then **On / Active** (843 LS 90, 750 LVZ). The profile's left aux sets On directly; if the system does not arm, use Start in the cab first.",
                "Check the signal, close the doors, release the brake."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "callout",
          "title": "Remember:",
          "text": "The lower yellow lamp and the strips below it are the speed at this signal; the upper lamp tells you what the next signal shows."
        }
      ]
